<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caracas</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Santiago de León de Caracas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caracas is the capital and largest city of Venezuela, in a mountain valley near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-losada">Diego de Losada</a> in 1567 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de León de Caracas, it became the seat of the province of Venezuela and in 1777 of the Captaincy General. The birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>, it led the independence movement from 1810, and it grew rapidly on oil wealth in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caracas.jpg" alt="Caracas" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olga Berrios · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caracas_desde_el_%C3%A1vila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
